    },
    "entity": {
      "$bytes": "45a05fb74835422196e231ae97291297"
    },
    "from": {
      "$bytes": "c050382dc2614403916342d43d2ef87a"
    },
    "to": {
      "$bytes": "03ab7fe708d646adb8ce086ea9e26b02"
    },
    "relationType": {
      "$bytes": "49c5d5e1679a4dbdbfd33f618f227c94"
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "updateEntity",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "2700dd4c50a641658f29fbc176d87f31"
    },
    "set": [
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "a126ca530c8e48d5b88882c734c38935"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "STAR does not justify across-the-board class-size reductions.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "9b1f76ff9711404c861e59dc3fa7d037"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Hanushek (2002) argues that broad reductions are too costly for the benefits established by existing evidence. He allows that reductions can be worthwhile in particular circumstances.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "unset": []
  },
  {
    "type": "createRelation",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "86ee00ccb4eb4d529e1c666c09328403"
    },
    "entity": {
      "$bytes": "860edf93c0714404a05b6831f37128d0"
    },
    "from": {
      "$bytes": "2700dd4c50a641658f29fbc176d87f31"
    },
    "to": {
      "$bytes": "96f859efa1ca4b229372c86ad58b694b"
    },
    "relationType": {
      "$bytes": "8f151ba4de204e3c9cb499ddf96f48f1"
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "updateEntity",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "2700dd4c50a641658f29fbc176d87f31"
    },
    "set": [
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "da4a6c1f9d4446f9832ff3b49a4400ef"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "value": false
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "84dacbddca6a44079edb5e11a4c66b40"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Chapter 2, Conclusions, printed p. 61",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "unset": []
  },
  {
    "type": "createRelation",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "ebb68a2942d54761a3f520e29a11340d"
    },
    "entity": {
      "$bytes": "9c8cbb208da3482e80e635954e53e321"
    },
    "from": {
      "$bytes": "2700dd4c50a641658f29fbc176d87f31"
    },
    "to": {
      "$bytes": "03ab7fe708d646adb8ce086ea9e26b02"
    },
    "relationType": {
      "$bytes": "49c5d5e1679a4dbdbfd33f618f227c94"
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "updateEntity",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "dc9f8289b4c94ed2b89c3e8f913f6d1e"
    },
    "set": [
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "a126ca530c8e48d5b88882c734c38935"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Projected earnings alone are too uncertain to justify large class-size reductions.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "9b1f76ff9711404c861e59dc3fa7d037"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Hanushek (2002) challenges the compounded assumptions connecting early test gains to lifetime earnings. He also argues that policy choices must consider alternatives such as improving teacher quality.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "unset": []
  },
  {
    "type": "createRelation",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "61c16fa3ea1b4bc5bf41a94a1b53bcf2"
    },
    "entity": {
      "$bytes": "eb87033a0aec45ceb7cda676ea950068"
    },
    "from": {
      "$bytes": "dc9f8289b4c94ed2b89c3e8f913f6d1e"
    },
    "to": {
      "$bytes": "96f859efa1ca4b229372c86ad58b694b"
    },
    "relationType": {
      "$bytes": "8f151ba4de204e3c9cb499ddf96f48f1"
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "updateEntity",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "dc9f8289b4c94ed2b89c3e8f913f6d1e"
    },
    "set": [
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "da4a6c1f9d4446f9832ff3b49a4400ef"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "value": false
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "84dacbddca6a44079edb5e11a4c66b40"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Chapter 2, Policy calculations, printed pp. 58–60",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "unset": []
  },
  {
    "type": "createRelation",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "447b708cafde4f21833a87c068137ec9"
    },
    "entity": {
      "$bytes": "5d78aee3adf849fa8ee377c38096e5d0"
    },
    "from": {
      "$bytes": "dc9f8289b4c94ed2b89c3e8f913f6d1e"
    },
    "to": {
      "$bytes": "03ab7fe708d646adb8ce086ea9e26b02"
    },
    "relationType": {
      "$bytes": "49c5d5e1679a4dbdbfd33f618f227c94"
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "updateEntity",
    "id": {
      "$bytes": "4b70147b5e53405590e4534fdd017eca"
    },
    "set": [
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "a126ca530c8e48d5b88882c734c38935"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "STAR’s early gains do not establish benefits from smaller classes in later grades.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "9b1f76ff9711404c861e59dc3fa7d037"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Hanushek (2002) interprets STAR’s advantage as concentrated at initial entry into small classes. He disputes extrapolation to later grades or smaller reductions, rather than claiming that no students benefit.",
          "language": {
